{
  "id": "typescript-14-declare-module-augmentation",
  "slug": "declare-module-augmentation",
  "title": "declare module and module augmentation",
  "moduleId": "typescript-14-modules-and-declarations",
  "order": 5,
  "hook": "**Module augmentation** extends third-party types — Express `Request.userId`, Jest custom matchers — via `declare module \"exact-name\" { interface ... }`.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "**declare module** merges with existing module declaration. Works on **interfaces** (declaration merging), not type aliases. Must import/reference base module. Side-effect import augmentation file in entry."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "module augmentation",
              "longForm": "declare module merge",
              "plainDefinition": "Add to existing module types.",
              "example": "declare module \"express-serve-static-core\""
            },
            {
              "term": "declaration merging",
              "longForm": "interface merge",
              "plainDefinition": "Same interface name merges.",
              "example": "interface User { a } + { b }"
            },
            {
              "term": "side-effect import",
              "longForm": "import \"./types\"",
              "plainDefinition": "Loads augmentation into graph.",
              "example": "import \"./express.d.ts\""
            },
            {
              "term": "exact module id",
              "longForm": "resolution string",
              "plainDefinition": "Must match import resolution.",
              "example": "\"express-serve-static-core\" not \"Express\""
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Auth middleware req.user typing. Jest matcher extensions. Wrong module string — silent no merge. C# extension methods are runtime."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: augment type alias",
          "body": "type aliases cannot be augmented — interfaces only."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "import base module",
              "body": "activate in graph"
            },
            {
              "title": "declare module exact id",
              "body": "match resolution"
            },
            {
              "title": "extend interface",
              "body": "inside block"
            },
            {
              "title": "side-effect import",
              "body": "app entry"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Augmentation merge",
            "source": "flowchart LR\n  ORIG[@types/express] --> AUG[your augment]\n  AUG --> MERGED[Merged Request]"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Express Request",
            "code": "import \"express-serve-static-core\";\ndeclare module \"express-serve-static-core\" { interface Request { userId?: string; } }\nfunction h(req: import(\"express\").Request) { console.log(req.userId); }",
            "explanation": "Standard Express pattern."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Jest matchers",
            "code": "declare global { namespace jest { interface Matchers<R> { toBeWithinRange(a: number, b: number): R; } } }",
            "explanation": "Custom matcher types."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Library consumer extend",
            "code": "declare module \"my-lib\" { interface Config { debug?: boolean; } }",
            "explanation": "Ship augmentation for consumers."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: wrong name",
            "code": "declare module \"Express\" { interface Request { x: string } } // no merge",
            "explanation": "Case/name must match resolution."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
